WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.940
Sovereign AI systems are often built to keep more control over models, data, infrastructure, and workflows.

2
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:16.200
They may run on local workstations, private servers, isolated networks, managed internal platforms, or hybrid environments.

3
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.700
That control is valuable, but it does not remove the need for monitoring.

4
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:30.080
A private system can still fail, slow down, leak too much telemetry, drift from its intended behavior, or become hard to explain after an incident.

5
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:35.480
Monitoring and logging provide the evidence needed to operate responsibly.

6
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:48.300
Teams need to know whether model services are available, whether retrieval systems are healthy, whether hardware is overloaded, whether data boundaries are being respected, and whether users and automation are acting within approved workflows.

7
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.540
Observability should not mean collecting everything.

8
00:00:51.640 --> 00:01:00.040
Prompts, outputs, retrieved content, tool arguments, file paths, and identifiers may contain sensitive information.

9
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:11.580
A sovereign AI monitoring strategy should collect the right evidence for reliability, privacy, performance, review, and accountability while avoiding unnecessary copies of the workload.

10
00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.820
The main telemetry types each answer different questions.

11
00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.000
Logs explain events.

12
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.260
Metrics show trends and health.

13
00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:22.320
Traces connect steps across a workflow.

14
00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.580
Audit records support accountability.

15
00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.680
Alerts call for action.

16
00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:30.780
Dashboards support review, and operational notes capture decisions.

17
00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:33.380
The foundation is restraint with purpose.

18
00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:43.800
Design telemetry before sensitive workflows begin, connect each signal to a real operational question, and treat monitoring data as part of the system's governance surface.
